            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ncl.2010.10.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Headache, and in particular, migraine, is often associated with comorbid psychiatric illness. The complex relationships between these disorders are slowly becoming understood. Successful management requires an integrated approach of neurologic and psychiatric management.</AbstractText>
